Apple Silicon: keep the JIT write protection correct across hooks running in a foreign runtime

Unicorn 2.1.x caches the per-thread MAP_JIT write protection in uc->current_executable,
skips pthread_jit_write_protect_np() whenever the cache already matches, and restores the
caller's state only when the outermost API call returns. Hook callbacks that run in a
runtime toggling the same per-thread state -- a JVM does so on every JNI transition --
break both assumptions:

1. A uc_* call made from the hook (uc_mem_unmap, uc_ctl_remove_cache, a nested
   uc_emu_start, ...) starts with the thread in execute mode while the cache still says
   write mode. The unlock before touching translated code is skipped and the write faults:

     SIGBUS in do_tb_phys_invalidate <- tb_invalidate_phys_page_range__locked
            <- uc_invalidate_tb <- memory_unmap_arm <- uc_mem_unmap   (from UC_HOOK_INTR)

2. When that nested call returns, the thread can be left in write mode. HotSpot resumes
   Java code without re-enabling execute permission for its code cache, so the JVM faults
   on the next instruction fetch in the calling Java method.

Fix:
- tb_exec_change() always applies the requested state instead of trusting the cache.
- restore_jit_state() hands the thread back in its entry state on every nesting level,
  not only the outermost one.
- uc_emu_start() saves/restores the state for nested calls too (they are made from
  hooks), including its two early-return error paths.

Only Apple arm64 builds change behaviour (__APPLE__ && HAVE_PTHREAD_JIT_PROTECT &&
__aarch64__); elsewhere save_jit_state()/restore_jit_state() are no-ops.

diff --git a/qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c b/qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
index 71b6b2b1..39edca40 100644
--- a/qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
+++ b/qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
@@ -2180,12 +2180,8 @@ static bool tb_exec_is_locked(struct uc_struct *uc)
 
 static void tb_exec_change(struct uc_struct *uc, bool executable)
 {
-    assert_executable(uc->current_executable);
-    if (uc->current_executable != executable) {
-        jit_write_protect(executable);
-        uc->current_executable = executable;
-        assert_executable(executable);
-    }
+    jit_write_protect(executable);
+    uc->current_executable = executable;
 }
 #else /* not needed on non-Darwin platforms */
 static bool tb_exec_is_locked(struct uc_struct *uc)
diff --git a/uc.c b/uc.c
index 75b89a01..ced6f76f 100644
--- a/uc.c
+++ b/uc.c
@@ -50,16 +50,11 @@ static void save_jit_state(uc_engine *uc)
